[32m+[m[32mj# PlasmaSimulator — Frontend/Backend Integration Contract[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is the shared contract for connecting `frontend/` to `backend/`. The interface currently uses local sample values; replace that state with these API responses without renaming JSON properties or changing units.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Canonical simulation parameters[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse the exact **camelCase** names and numeric base units below in requests, responses, database records, and live-update messages.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Property | Meaning | Unit | Example |[m
[32m+[m[32m| --- | --- | --- | --- |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `magneticField` | Applied field, B0 | tesla (`T`) | `2.4` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `electronDensity` | Electron density, ne | `10^19 m^-3` | `4.8` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `electronTemperature` | Electron temperature, Te | electronvolt (`eV`) | `125` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `ionTemperature` | Ion temperature, Ti | electronvolt (`eV`) | `38` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `chamberRadius` | Chamber radius, R | metre (`m`) | `0.42` |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll five values are JSON numbers—never display strings such as `"2.4 T"`. Do not silently use `m^-3` for `electronDensity`; if required internally, expose it separately as `electronDensityPerCubicMeter`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## IDs, status, and time[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* `simulationId`: string (UUID recommended).[m
[32m+[m[32m* `status`: one of `idle`, `queued`, `running`, `paused`, `completed`, `failed`.[m
[32m+[m[32m* `elapsedSeconds`: number in seconds. The UI displays microseconds: `elapsedSeconds * 1_000_000`.[m
[32m+[m[32m* `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `startedAt`, `completedAt`: ISO-8601 UTC strings.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Keep `schemaVersion` (start at `1`) in saved simulation and result payloads. Add optional properties instead of repurposing existing ones.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## REST API proposal[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBase path: `/api/v1`; use `Content-Type: application/json`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Create run[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`POST /simulations`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```json[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m  "schemaVersion": 1,[m
[32m+[m[32m  "parameters": {[m
[32m+[m[32m    "magneticField": 2.4,[m
[32m+[m[32m    "electronDensity": 4.8,[m
[32m+[m[32m    "electronTemperature": 125,[m
[32m+[m[32m    "ionTemperature": 38,[m
[32m+[m[32m    "chamberRadius": 0.42[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mReturn `201` with the saved simulation including `simulationId`, `status`, timestamps, and the unchanged `parameters` object.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Run controls and results[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* `POST /simulations/:simulationId/actions` with `{ "action": "start" | "pause" | "reset" }`; return the updated simulation. Reset sets `elapsedSeconds` to `0` and status to `idle`.[m
[32m+[m[32m* `GET /simulations/:simulationId` returns the saved simulation including `parameters`, `status`, and `elapsedSeconds`.[m
[32m+[m[32m* `GET /simulations/:simulationId/results` returns a `metrics` object containing `particleCount` (count), `peakDensity` (`10^19 m^-3`), and `energyConfinementMs` (milliseconds). Use `null` for unavailable metrics, not a text placeholder.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Error and merge rules[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse `{ "error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "...", "fields": { "electronDensity": "Must be >= 0" } } }`. Return `400` for invalid inputs, `404` unknown IDs, `409` invalid state changes, and `500` server failures. Permit `http://localhost:4200` via CORS for local development.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore merging, validate that all five parameters are finite and non-negative, keep the API base URL in one frontend config value (not a component), and agree on polling or a `simulation.updated` WebSocket/SSE event. Update this document before changing a field, unit, status, or response shape.[m
